  "claim_scope": "An elementary, exact representational obstruction: for each checked palette q, this projection requires a clause of width q*(q-1)/2 in auxiliary-free CNF over terminal-pair color equality/disequality predicates. At fixed q=5 this rules out widths below ten, including width two. A bound uniform over the general q family fails when BOTH palette size and terminal count grow. No novelty claim, Boolean 2-SAT claim, algorithmic running-time lower bound, graph-coloring complexity separation, or P-versus-NP conclusion is made.",
  "experiment": "projection_barrier",
  "fixed_palette_limit": "This star family does not rule out every fixed clause width while the palette remains five colors and only the number of terminals grows. Its five-color example has an exact width-ten clause.",
